d(f(x) - f(x_0)) = d(f(x) - f_n(x) + f_n(x) - f_n(x_0) + f_n(v_0) - f(x_0))
\]
\[
\leq d(f_n(x) - f(x) + d(f_n(x) - f_n(v_0)) + d(f_n(x) - f(x_0))
\]
\[
\leq \frac{\epsilon}{3} + \frac{\epsilon}{3} + \frac{\epsilon}{3} \quad \forall n \geq \max\{N_1, N_2\}
\]
\[
\leq \frac{\epsilon}{3}
\]
$\therefore f$ is continuous at $x_0$.

