(1) Sol$m$:-

As per given question; $\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i = \cos(\alpha_i) \quad [1 \le i \le m]$

and, $\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i$ denotes length of the projection of $\hat{u}$ onto $\hat{v}_i$

So, by definition; $\|\hat{u}\| = \sqrt{(\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_1)^2 + (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_2)^2 + \dots + (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_m)^2}$

$\Rightarrow \|\hat{u}\|^2 = \cos^2(\alpha_1) + \cos^2(\alpha_2) + \dots + \cos^2(\alpha_m)$

$\Rightarrow \sum_{i=1}^{m} \cos^2(\alpha_i) = 1 \quad [\because \|\hat{u}\| = 1]$

then, $1 + \sin^2\alpha_1 + \dots + \sin^2\alpha_m$

$= 1 + (1 - \cos^2\alpha_1) + \dots + (1 - \cos^2\alpha_m)$

$= 1 + m - \sum_{i=1}^{m} \cos^2(\alpha_i)$

$= 1 + m - 1$

$= m$ (Proved)

