$\vec{v}$ along line $L = \frac{v_\theta [\cos\theta, \sin\theta]}{\sqrt{\cos^2\theta + \sin^2\theta}} \times [\cos\theta, \sin\theta]$

$\Rightarrow [v_\theta [\cos\theta, \sin\theta]] (\cos\theta, \sin\theta)$

$\Rightarrow (x_1 \cos\theta + y_1 \sin\theta) [\cos\theta, \sin\theta]$.

$\therefore$ Reflection = $2(\text{proj } v \text{ along } L) - \vec{v}$

$= \frac{[2x_1 \cos\theta + 2y_1 \sin\theta]}{\text{scalar}} \frac{(\cos\theta, \sin\theta) - (x_1, y_1)}{\text{Direction vector}} - \vec{v}$

$T_1 = \begin{bmatrix} (2x_1 \cos\theta_1 + 2y_1 \sin\theta_1) \cos\theta_1 - x_1 \\ (2x_1 \cos\theta_1 + 2y_1 \sin\theta_1) \sin\theta_1 - y_1 \end{bmatrix}$

$T_2 = \begin{bmatrix} (2x_1 \cos\theta_2 + 2y_1 \sin\theta_2) \cos\theta_2 - x_1 \\ (2x_1 \cos\theta_2 + 2y_1 \sin\theta_2) \sin\theta_2 - y_1 \end{bmatrix}$

