\noindent\textbf{(b)} In $\mathbb{R}^2$, let
\begin{align*}
B^2 &= \{(x,y) \mid x^2 + y^2 \leq 1\}, \qquad C_1 = \{(x,y) \mid (x-2)^2 + y^2 = 1\} \\
C_2 &= \{(x,y) \mid (x+2)^2 + y^2 = 1\}, \qquad C_3 = \{(x,y) \mid x^2 + y^2 = 9\}
\end{align*}

\vspace{0.5em}

\noindent Find a continuous $g : \mathbb{R}^2 \to \mathbb{R}$, such that $g(v) = 7$ if and only if $v \in B^2 \cup C_1 \cup C_2 \cup C_3$.

