Given $\{\hat{v}_1, \hat{v}_2, \ldots, \hat{v}_n\}$ is an orthonormal Basis for $\mathbb{R}^n$

$\Rightarrow \|\hat{v}_i\| = 1$ and $\hat{u}$ is a unit vector $\in \mathbb{R}^n$.

$\hat{v}_i \cdot \hat{v}_j = 0$ \quad [$\because$ it is orthonormal Basis]

$\hat{u} \cdot x$ \quad let $\hat{u} = (u_1, u_2, \ldots, u_n)$

$\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i = u_j$ \quad (it covers every components of $u$ at some $i$)

$\Rightarrow \sum_{i=1}^{n} (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i)^2 = \sum_{j=1}^{n} u_j^2 = \|\hat{u}\|^2 = 1$ \quad \textbf{---(1)}

$\alpha_i \rightarrow \text{arg}^n$ \quad between $\hat{u}$ and $\hat{v}_i$

$\cos \alpha_i = \dfrac{\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i}{\|\hat{u}\| \cdot \|\hat{v}_i\|} = \hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i$

$\sum_{i=1}^{n} \cos^2 \alpha_i = \sum_{i=1}^{n} (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i)^2 = 1$ \quad [from (1)]

$\therefore \cos^2 \alpha_1 + \cos^2 \alpha_2 + \cdots + \cos^2 \alpha_n = 1 \Rightarrow (1 - \sin^2 \alpha_1) + (1 - \sin^2 \alpha_2) + \cdots + (1 - \sin^2 \alpha_n) = 1$

$\therefore \boxed{1 + \sin^2 \alpha_1 + \sin^2 \alpha_2 + \cdots + \sin^2 \alpha_n = n}$

$\sum (1 - \sin^2 \alpha_i) = 1 \Rightarrow \boxed{1 + \sin^2 \alpha_1 + \sin^2 \alpha_2 + \cdots + \sin^2 \alpha_n = n}$

