\vspace{0.3cm}

\noindent $A_{2 \times 2}^{-1} = \dfrac{\text{adj } A_{2 \times 2}}{|A_{2 \times 2}|} = \dfrac{1}{a_{11} \cdot a_{22}} \begin{bmatrix} a_{11} & a_{12} \\ 0 & a_{22} \end{bmatrix}$, \quad it is upper triangular matrix

\vspace{0.3cm}

\noindent Now, for, $A_{3 \times 3} = \begin{bmatrix} a_{11} & a_{12} & a_{13} \\ 0 & a_{22} & a_{23} \\ 0 & 0 & a_{33} \end{bmatrix}$, \quad $\text{adj } A_{3 \times 3} = \begin{bmatrix} \text{Cofactor } A_{3 \times 3} \end{bmatrix}^{T}$

