\noindent (1) \underline{Solm:-}

As per given question; $\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i = \cos(\alpha_i) \quad [1 \leq i \leq n]$

and, $\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_i$ denotes length of the projection of $\hat{u}$ onto $\hat{v}_i$

So, by definition; $\|\hat{u}\| = \sqrt{(\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_1)^2 + (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_2)^2 + \cdots + (\hat{u} \cdot \hat{v}_n)^2}$

$\Rightarrow \|\hat{u}\|^2 = \cos^2(\alpha_1) + \cos^2(\alpha_2) + \cdots + \cos^2(\alpha_m)$

$\Rightarrow \sum_{i=1}^{m} \cos^2(\alpha_i) = 1 \quad \left[\because \|\hat{u}\| = 1\right]$

then, $1 + \sin^2\alpha_1 + \cdots + \sin^2\alpha_m$

\begin{align*}
&= 1 + (1 - \cos^2\alpha_1) + \cdots + (1 - \cos^2\alpha_m) \\
&= 1 + m - \sum_{i=1}^{m} \cos^2(\alpha_i) \\
&= 1 + m - 1 \\
&= m \quad (\text{Proved})
\end{align*}

