Since $\vec{v} = \vec{v_0} + \vec{v_1}$ where $\vec{v_0} \in S$ and $\vec{v_1} \in S^{\perp}$, we can say that $\vec{v_0} = \text{Proj}_{\vec{w}}(\vec{v})$

