    \item If $m \leq n$ the solution has dimension $n - \text{rank}(A)$

    \item If $m > n$ and full rank, then the only solution is the trivial solution so, $\dim(S) = 0$

    \item The maximum possible dimension of the solution space is $n$, so if $\dim(S) > n$ it is not correct (incorrect)
\end{itemize}

